  "title": "U.S. Suspend Microsoft, Adobe, and IT Firms from Green Card Program",
  "summary": "The U.S. Labor Department has suspended Cognizant, Infosys, Tata, Wipro, HCL, Capgemini, and Microsoft from the permanent labor certification program, citing multiple federal investigations related to their participation in the program. This extension is part of a broader political and economic conflict, with India facing challenges due to the administration's policies.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. Labor Department suspended Cognizant, Infosys, Tata, Wipro, HCL, Capgemini, and Microsoft from the permanent labor certification program.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Microsoft's suspension is linked to allegations of abuse of the H-1B visa program, with Vice President JD Vance accusing the company of exploiting the system.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Microsoft reported 80% of its H-1B visa applications were to extend or change the status of existing employees.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
